<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inca Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Inca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Inca Empire was the largest state in pre-Columbian America, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> in the Andes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. It was conquered by Spanish forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> from 1532. Its gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and its territory became central to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inca-empire.jpg" alt="Inca Empire" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Made and uploaded by Huhsunqu. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Inca_Empire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
